21. Final acceptance criteria

The work is complete only when all of the following are true:

1. Horizontal Knockback Power no longer exists.
2. Vertical Knockback Power no longer exists.
3. powers.js contains no attack Knockback system.
4. No ordinary attack declares horizontalKnockback or verticalKnockback.
5. No old attack Knockback tier resolver remains.
6. A standalone Low/Mid/High Knockback registry/resolver exists.
7. Low/Mid/High preserve the former tier-1/2/3 magnitudes:
    horizontal 140/180/220 and vertical 480/640/800.
8. Ground BA1 declares Low horizontal Knockback and resolves to { x: 140, y: 0 }.
9. Ground BA2 declares High vertical Knockback and resolves to { x: 0, y: 800 }.
10. Final Mid-air BA1 declares Mid reversed vertical Knockback and resolves to { x: 0, y: -640 }.
11. Final Mid-air BA2 declares Low vertical Knockback and resolves to { x: 0, y: 480 }.
12. An actual Mid-air BA1 hit gives the opponent positive vy and drives it downward.
13. An actual BA2 hit gives the opponent vy === -800.
14. Ground BA1 still reverses horizontal velocity correctly with fighter facing.
15. Mid-air BA1 and Mid-air BA2 have completely exchanged their previous airborne move identities.
16. The final midairBa1 uses the former midair2ba 3-frame kunai/slash artwork and corresponding move package.
17. The final midairBa2 uses the former midair1ba 5-frame kick artwork and corresponding move package.
18. action1.air still semantically starts midairBa1.
19. action2.air still semantically starts midairBa2.
20. The shuriken remains zero knockback.
21. Clone Attack inherits ground BA1’s new Low horizontal Knockback.
22. Jump Power and Speed Power remain unchanged.
23. Discover’s Power page contains only the remaining Powers.
24. Discover exposes Knockback Low/Mid/High as its own mechanic rather than as Powers.
25. There are no stale old Knockback Power names in production code, tests, README, or ALVA_SPEC.md.
26. Relevant targeted tests pass.
27. The complete Node test suite passes.

Run the focused Knockback, Power, BA1, BA2, Discover, Clone, Throw, and Practice tests first. Then run the complete test suite.

